Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 02:56:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dcp): order hard-BLOCKED checks before UNKNOWN-authority
 guard (PRE-P6-0002)

_derive_route_status checked has_unknown_authority before the BLOCKED-authority,
missing-proof, and stale-proof gates, so a hard-BLOCKED reason was masked as
RouteStatus.UNKNOWN whenever authority was also unknown (the conservative default).
The reason was still in stop_conditions, but status -- the field callers inspect to
learn *why* a route is blocked -- reported UNKNOWN.

Reorder to most-severe-first (BLOCKED > UNKNOWN): the hard-BLOCKED checks now run
before the UNKNOWN-authority guard. Not a security change -- an unknown-authority
route is non-runnable regardless (is_runnable() unchanged); this only surfaces the
real reason in status. Red-lane is still derived first, so MCP/live-write/dopetask/
secrets hard-blocks are unaffected.

TDD red->green: dropped the has_unknown_authority=False bypass from the 0002R
stale-proof test + added precedence and no-over-block guardrail tests.

Validation: compileall PASS; tests/unit/dcp/ 178 pass; +tests/dcp 0001 domain = 193 pass;
classifier file 77 pass; git diff --check clean. Embedded audit (independent Opus): PASS
-- 41,472-combo exhaustive sweep, 0 newly-runnable, 0 UNKNOWN->ALLOWED, 0 allowed_actions
broadening, no counterexample.

Resolves the precedence bug deferred from 0002R reconciliation (#902).

